CORE
concat.json_symtab
_ --function main --no-simplify --trace
^string built-in 'cprover_string_concat_func' is not supported by the bit-vector back-end and is treated as an uninterpreted function, which may yield spurious counterexamples; use an SMT back-end \(e.g., --z3 or --cvc5\)$
^EXIT=(0|10)$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^Invariant check failed
--
The bit-vector back-end does not interpret string built-ins over SMT-LIB
strings, and must say so. The verdict and the trace values are those of an
uninterpreted function, and therefore not checked. --no-simplify avoids
symex constant propagation of the string operation.
